    {
      "description": "After each user message, send the exchange here so it can be remembered. You do not need to decide what is important — just forward the user message (and your reply, if you have one) and Synap will keep what matters. If your app serves more than one end-user, pass that person's stable id as user_id (or an organization id as customer_id) so each person's memory stays separate; if every conversation is the same single user, omit them. Logging is fire-and-forget by default; set wait_for_processing=true only when you need to confirm the memory finished extracting before continuing.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "properties": {
          "assistant_message": {
            "default": "",
            "title": "Assistant Message",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "conversation_id": {
